   "text": {
    "L1": "A state and a government are connected, but they are not the same thing.",
    "L2": "A state has people, territory, a government and sovereignty. The state is lasting, while governments can change after elections.",
    "L3": "So a new government does not make a new state. The people, territory and sovereignty remain.",
    "L4": "Government has three organs. The legislature makes laws, the executive carries them out, and the judiciary interprets laws and settles disputes.",
    "L5": "Government works at three levels: Union, state and local. Different jobs fit different levels.",
    "L6": "The Union handles defence and railways. States handle police and many schools and hospitals.",
    "L7": "Local bodies handle services such as water, streetlights and cleanliness. For a local pothole, report it and follow up with the local body.",
    "L8": "Government affects daily life through documents and services, and taxes help pay for them. Citizens also shape government by voting and speaking up peacefully."
   },
